## Self-Heal: Failure Analyst Summary
Root cause: Validation process.exit(2) calls are inside try/catch that catches the mock's thrown error and re-exits with code 1.
Fix: Do NOT wrap argument validation process.exit(2) calls inside the same try/catch that handles runtime errors — the test mocks process.exit to throw, and the catch block will swallow exit code 2 and re-exit with code 1. Place validation before the try/catch block, or re-throw errors whose message matches /^EXIT_CODE_/ in the catch handler.
